From d877db46936d12b9c4843546698017a066f34b99 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 25 Jul 2026 08:28:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Two more ways to get a usable frame
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Stock footage no longer depends on one library, and the image studio can
ask for a photograph instead of hoping for one.

Wikimedia Commons joins the stock registry as a keyless source, restricted
to public domain and CC0 files — CC-BY is excluded because a published post
has nowhere to put the attribution, and CC-BY-SA because share-alike could
follow the tenant's finished video out the door. It is failover, not a
substitute: it only joins the auto list when a keyed library is configured,
so a fresh deployment still gets the loud "add a Pexels key" 400. Ordering
runs through the health breaker across both groups, so a healthy Commons
beats a broken Pexels and a healthy Pexels still wins outright. Tenants can
also pick it outright.

The runtime now actually walks that list. gatherStockClips searched one
source and gave up; collectStockCandidates tries each in turn and moves on
when a source comes back empty, which covers both "the API is down" and
"this library has nothing for monsoon street food" — from the caller's seat
those are the same problem with the same answer. Preflight walks the same
list, so it can neither refuse a job the runtime would have served nor fund
one the runtime will reject.

The image Look pills compile a brief into photographic direction: a genre
preset carries the boring correct gear for that shoot (macro at f/8 on a
sweep for packshots, 35mm by a window for lifestyle) and each axis can be
overridden on its own. It is a lookup and a join — no model call, no key,
no cost, same recipe in, same string out. Compiling happens in the routes so
the stored prompt is the finished text the gallery can replay, which is also
why there is no schema change and no runner change.

